/* cc_gallery.rasi — icon-grid theme for the Control Center's wallpaper
   gallery page (page_wallgallery), ported from the old standalone
   rofi/gallery.rasi picker.

   MECHANISM (no rofi relaunch): rofi 2.0 script mode lets every invocation
   carry a small theme snippet via the "\0theme\x1f<snippet>" mode option
   (rofi-script(5)). control_center.sh reads THIS file when the current page
   is Wallgallery, strips comments and @import lines, collapses it to a
   single line and emits it as that snippet — the theme of the RUNNING
   Control Center updates in place. Every other page emits CC_LIST_THEME
   (defined in control_center.sh, mirrors cc_theme.rasi) so leaving the
   gallery restores the list layout; keep the two in sync with cc_theme.rasi.

   NOTE: rofi-script(5) warns the per-call snippet cannot restructure the
   interface, only update existing widgets. These property updates degrade
   acceptably if geometry does not re-layout live: 3 columns of 160px icon
   tiles also fit inside the default 640px-wide window.

   Old-grid values (rofi/gallery.rasi): 85% window, 4 columns x 3 lines,
   220px icons, vertical elements, hidden text. Ported here as 3x4 with
   160px icons and visible labels: the CC gallery shares its listview with
   the "← Tabs" row and the filter inputbar, so labels stay readable and
   tiles fit both the 85% and the 640px window. */

@import "~/.config/rofi/colors.rasi"

window {
    width: 85%;
}

listview {
    columns:          3;
    lines:            4;
    fixed-height:     true;
    spacing:          8px;
}

element {
    orientation:      vertical;
    spacing:          6px;
    padding:          4px;
    border-radius:    10px;
    background-color: transparent;
}

element selected.normal {
    background-color: @accent-subtle;
    border:           2px solid;
    border-color:     @accent;
    text-color:       @accent-subtle-fg;
}

element-icon {
    size:             160px;
    cursor:           pointer;
}

element-text {
    horizontal-align: 0.5;
    cursor:           pointer;
}
